      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-64223",
      ":question/problem": "A particle of mass $5kg$ is attached to a massless spring. The spring constant associated with the spring is $k = 20kg/s^{2}$. The position of the particle is $y(t)$ (measured in meters), and $t > 0$ is the time in seconds.\n\nIf the particle moves with simple harmonic motion, then which of the following statements are true?\n\n1. The governing differential equation is $y^{\u2033} + 4y = 0$\n2. The frequency $f$ of the oscillation is $f = \\frac{2}{\u03c0}s^{-1}$\n3. The general solution can be expressed as $y = R\\cos (2t + \u03d5)$, where $R$ is the amplitude and $\u03d5$ is the phase."
